# .cursor/rules/project-rules.mdc — GitContextGen AI Guidelines

> **Single Source of Truth**: Synchronized with [CLAUDE.md](../../CLAUDE.md) and [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md).
> Cursor agent rules are enforced globally via `alwaysApply: true`.

You are an expert full-stack developer working on GitContextGen (RepoPulse AI).

## 1. Tech Stack & Execution Commands
- Framework: Next.js 16.2.12 (Turbopack, App Router, React 19)
- Runtime: Cloudflare Workers Edge via OpenNext (@opennextjs/cloudflare)
- Dev Server: `npm run dev`
- Verification / Typecheck: `npx tsc --noEmit`
- Production Build: `npm run build`
- Deploy to Cloudflare: `npm run deploy`
- MCP Server Build: `npm run build` (in mcp-server/)

## 2. Strict Architectural Rules
- [Next.js App Router] Always write Server Components by default. Mark interactive UI with 'use client' at top of file.
- [Edge Runtime] Cloudflare Workers compatibility (workerd). Avoid unsupported Node.js native bindings in edge route handlers.
- [Security] Mermaid.js must always use `securityLevel: 'strict'`. Never log or commit API keys or .env files.
- [MCP Protocol] Tool definitions must adhere strictly to @modelcontextprotocol/sdk schemas with runtime input validation and persistent L1/L2 caching.

## 3. Strict Backend Code Freeze & Modification Protocol (STRICT FREEZE)
- **Protected Core Pipeline**: The backend analysis engine, API route handlers, MCP memory pipelines, secret sanitization logic, and caching layers are production-ready and under strict code freeze.
  - `src/app/api/analyze/route.ts` & `src/app/api/webhooks/**/*.ts`
  - `src/lib/analyzer/**/*.ts` & `src/lib/sanitizer/**/*.ts` (and secret redaction)
  - `src/lib/mcp/**/*.ts` & `src/lib/locks/**/*.ts` (and `fileLock.ts`)
  - `src/lib/cacheStore.ts` & `src/lib/db.ts`
- **Mandatory Approval Protocol**:
  1. **Stop & Flag**: Never touch protected files without explicit developer sign-off.
  2. **Impact Assessment**: State why, which file/function, and any risks or breaking changes.
  3. **Explicit Query**: Ask: *"This change requires updating [File Path]. Should I proceed with modifying the backend processing logic, or can we accomplish this purely within the frontend presentation layer?"*
  4. **Proceed ONLY upon explicit written developer confirmation.**
- **Frontend Independence**: All new features, exports, or dashboard cards must consume existing backend API responses without altering core pipeline processing.